      "assignedTo": "Satya Siddhartha",
      "topic": "Sensors",
      "filterCategory": "Pipe & Acoustic",
      "citation": "See, C. H., Horoshenkov, K. V., Bin Ali, M. T., & Tait, S. J. (2021). An Acoustic Sensor for Combined Sewer Overflow Screen Condition Monitoring in a Drainage Infrastructure. Sensors, 21(2), 404. https://doi.org/10.3390/s21020404",
      "intro": "See et al. develop an autonomous acoustic transceiver system for continuous real-time monitoring of bar screen ragging in Combined Sewer Overflow (CSO) chambers.",
      "methods": "Designed an acoustic transmitter/receiver array measuring acoustic wave attenuation and frequency shifts as debris and wet wipes blind the CSO bar screen.",
      "scope": "CSO relief chambers, overflow bar screens, ragging detection, and remote alert generation.",
      "usefulness": "Directly solves the critical utility problem of fibrous ragging on overflow screens without requiring submerged probes that foul rapidly.",
