      "citation": "Prisutova, J., Krynkin, A., Tait, S., & Horoshenkov, K. (2022). Use of Fibre-Optic Sensors for Pipe Condition and Hydraulics Measurements: A Review. CivilEng, 3(1), 85–113. https://doi.org/10.3390/civileng3010006",
      "intro": "This review evaluates the application of distributed fiber-optic sensors (DTS and DAS) for sewer pipe condition assessment and continuous hydraulic monitoring.",
      "methods": "Examined Raman/Brillouin Distributed Temperature Sensing (DTS) and Rayleigh Distributed Acoustic Sensing (DAS) installed along sewer pipe inverts and crowns.",
