      "filterCategory": "Water Quality",
      "citation": "Helm, I., Karina, G., Jalukse, L., Pagano, T., & Leito, I. (2018). Comparative validation of amperometric and optical analyzers of dissolved oxygen: a case study. Environmental Monitoring and Assessment, 190, 313. https://doi.org/10.1007/s10661-018-6692-5",
      "intro": "Helm et al. rigorously compare the measurement uncertainty, calibration stability, and performance of optical luminescent DO (LDO) sensors versus electrochemical Clark polarographic cells.",
      "methods": "Conducted extensive ISO/IEC 17025 validation protocols, drift tests, and response time experiments on optical luminescence-quenching vs. amperometric dissolved oxygen analyzers in complex water matrices.",
      "scope": "Dissolved oxygen (DO) monitoring (0–20 mg/L), sulfide and toxic gas poisoning, calibration drift over time, and temperature compensation.",
